From 5930dd23e926de7463e3ce40ec1e7821b5cafed6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 78andyp <drandypowell@live.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:56:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [video] Add "Refresh all content" to the video source context
 menu

Refreshing a whole source previously meant opening the info dialog and
refreshing every movie, show or music video one at a time. The new
entry runs a job that refreshes every library item in the source,
including disc rips stored under encoded bluray:// or udf:// paths, with
the same refresh job the info dialog uses. It runs non-modally, so
matches are chosen automatically as during a scan and local NFOs are
used. TV shows are refreshed with all their episodes. Progress is shown
in the background progress bar, as for a library scan, and while it
runs the library counts as being scanned, so it is stopped with a scan.
The source's entry becomes "Stop refreshing" while it is refreshed.

An item whose media is missing is not refreshed, as the refresh would
remove it from the library, and is left to library cleaning instead.

The refresh job now bails out when no scraper is found for the item's
path, rather than dereferencing a null scraper, as happens when an
item's folder has been excluded since it was scanned.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
